      <activity id="1a8aee66-d03b-55c7-ae1d-872092e24ce3" activityNameId="5e02d9da-bb2c-5702-aa1f-c4ecb7982bba" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, powertrain, for electric scooter</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, powertrain, for electric scooter
This dataset describes the treatment of a used  electric drivetrain of an electric scooter. The original dataset has been developed for a drivetrain comprising an electric motor (5.8kg), a controller (1.27kg) and a charger (3.025). First, the drivetrain is manually dismantled to recover all large metal scrap, especially from the electric motor and from the cases of the electronic devices. The scrap steel, copper and aluminium directly recovered from the components is sent to the respective scrap recycling facilities, while the remaining electronics scrap is sent to a smelter facility.;
UUID: cedf5dd7-8a33-35a4-a87c-309d691ec658
The dataset starts with the electric drivetrain which needs to be dismantled already in the dismantling facility. The dataset returns the outcome scrap fractions for aluminium, steel, copper, plastic and waste electronics.
Location: data of situation in Switzerland
Technology: current manual dismantling activities in Switzerland.
Time period: Unspecified
Production volume: 7800000 kg
Sampling: Literature 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: &lt;null&gt;
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_cedf5dd7-8a33-35a4-a87c-309d691ec658.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
